@* -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   This host has no Razor components of its own - the Explorer's App root and all
   its interactive components ship inside the Orleans.Lattice.Explorer.Web hosting
   library (an RCL). Under the .NET 10 SDK a Web host with zero Razor content is
   not detected as a Blazor host, so the framework's _framework/blazor.web.js
   static asset is never contributed to the app: the console renders server-side
   but the interactive circuit never starts (Sign in does nothing, tabs stay
   greyed, capability probes never run, "Access to the state API was denied").

   The library ships a build props that sets RequiresAspNetWebAssets=true to force
   this, but that property alone no longer emits blazor.web.js on .NET 10. The
   reliable trigger is the presence of Razor content in the host itself, so this
   otherwise-empty _Imports.razor exists solely to make the SDK treat the host as
   a Blazor app and emit the framework script. Do not delete it.
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- *@
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components
